## Dead Ends
Upstream does not publish a selector training loss, initialization recipe, optimizer schedule, or convergence result. A top-K-hit-only loss was rejected because it produces almost no initial supervision. A FULL_SHARD fallback to model.state_dict was rejected because it can save local DTensor shards. Supporting mixed attention layouts, arbitrary Qwen activations or RoPE modes, and USP would require larger shared refactors. The old single-microbatch restriction was removed after main added pooled additive DFlash loss terms.

## Hints for Future Agents
The selector objective is a TorchSpec-defined sampled teacher-forced cross-entropy objective, not claimed upstream training parity. DFlash2Config must dispatch before DFlashConfig. Packed convolutions must reset at block boundaries. Official checkpoint codebook keys omit .weight. Serving writers must use cache_rank and synchronize errors before any rank raises. Do not restore a local FULL_SHARD state-dict fallback. Keep the selector as an additive numerator over the same objective denominator returned to DFlashTrainer so accumulation and data-parallel normalization happen once across the optimizer window. The verifier-norm path now comes from main and DFlash2 inherits it.

## Codebase Discoveries
DFlash PR 134 provides the extension seams through DFlashModel._draft_backbone and DFlashTrainer build hooks. Official DFlash2 uses a Qwen3-facing configuration with nested dflash_config fields. The public upstream repository contains inference code only. Mooncake has no macOS ARM wheel, so related CPU tests use an import-only stub and do not exercise transport. Trainer.cache_rank is global while Trainer.dp_rank can be a subgroup rank.

## Open Questions
